  "section_notes": "Final rules keep 55°C testing and give per-model results to customers/regulators but not the public, while allowing above-5% models to remain on sale with only corrective-action plans. Remote shut-off retrofit is set at 6 years, fire suppression at 36 months, and a mandatory recall trigger at 8/100k with prompt notice. The no-sales-stop S2 outcome and strict S5 trigger are the main deviations from the SAFE key, favoring Northwind overall."
